      "source": "WCAG 2.2 SC 1.3.5 Identify Input Purpose; HTML §4.10.18.7.1 autofill detail tokens",
      "applicability": "input (except type=hidden), select and textarea elements with an autocomplete attribute.",
      "expectation": "Fails when the autocomplete value does not follow the HTML autofill grammar\n[section-*] [shipping|billing] [home|work|mobile|fax|pager] field-name\n[webauthn], or is not on/off: an unknown field name (\"company\",\n\"delivery-note\"), a contact token before a non-contact field (\"work name\"),\ntokens in the wrong order (\"postal-code shipping\"). Case does not matter.\nValid combinations pass (\"section-parcel shipping street-address\", \"work\nemail\", \"mobile tel\", \"Shipping Country-Name\", \"off\"). type=hidden carries no\nuser input and is not judged.",
